Q4. Your message and your decision

Message sent to my assistant: “Help me plan a surprise birthday party for my friend. Give me a simple plan, ideas for decorations, games, food, and a suitable budget. Make the plan practical and easy to follow.”

The five stops I used were what I wanted, who it was for, what information I gave, what I asked, and what result I expected.

I decided the final budget and the activities myself because I know my friend’s preferences and what is possible for us.

Q5. Your check

Fact I checked: Whether the plan was practical and suitable for my budget.

Was it the right check, and why? Yes, because a birthday plan should be affordable and possible to arrange.

What would have gone wrong without checking? I might have chosen activities or decorations that were too expensive or difficult to arrange.

